    <header class="case__header">
      <div class="case__meta">CASE 01 &middot; DEPARTMENT OF HUMAN SERVICES &middot; BENEFITS ELIGIBILITY TOOL &middot; 2026</div>
      <div class="case__for">FOR: CASEWORKER &middot; 11 YEARS IN ROLE</div>
    </header>

    {# C.4.b · Stamp #}
    <div class="case__stamp">ILLUSTRATIVE &middot; HYPOTHETICAL ENGAGEMENT</div>

    {# C.4.c · Narrative (body prose stays title case for proper nouns) #}
    <div class="case__narrative">
      <p><span class="dropcap">E</span>very morning, a benefits caseworker at the Department of Human Services opens a tool she's been using for eleven years. Forty&#8209;seven main screens. Three hundred form fields. A navigation pattern she learned by trauma. No new hire inherits it without months of shadowing. The people she's approving or denying benefits to wait while she clicks through it.</p>

      <p>That's what we were asked to redesign.</p>

      <p>We didn't start with screens. We started by listing every object in the system: case, client, household, benefit, determination, task, document. Then we worked out which ones lived inside which. We interviewed caseworkers. We watched them work. We rewrote the list of things the tool needed to do. It was shorter than the list of things it was doing.</p>

      <p>The result was <span class="emph">uglier than the old version in some places.</span> It was also the first version a caseworker could teach her replacement in a single shift.</p>
    </div>

    {# C.4.d · Outcomes grid #}
    <div class="case__outcomes">
      <div class="outcomes__col outcomes__col--before">
        <span class="outcomes__label">BEFORE</span>
        <dl>
          <dt>Main screens</dt><dd>47</dd>
          <dt>Form fields</dt><dd>300</dd>
          <dt class="outcomes__key">Time to onboard</dt><dd>Six months</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="outcomes__col outcomes__col--after">
        <span class="outcomes__label">AFTER</span>
        <dl>
          <dt>Main screens</dt><dd>12</dd>
          <dt>Form fields</dt><dd>84</dd>
          <dt class="outcomes__key">Time to learn</dt><dd>One shift</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# C.4.e · Case pull-quote #}
    <div class="case__quote">
      <span class="label">The number that mattered</span>
      <p>The number that mattered was &ldquo;one shift.&rdquo; The screen count dropped because the screens were the wrong shape, not because fewer was the goal.</p>
    </div>

